## English

- Project: proxyscene
- Original repository: https://github.com/longlannet/proxyscene
- License: MIT License

The `proxyscene` manager statically links the following third-party Go modules.
Their complete license texts are distributed as `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`:

- **github.com/titanous/json5 v1.0.0**: BSD 3-Clause / MIT
- **golang.org/x/sys v0.47.0**: BSD 3-Clause
- **gopkg.in/yaml.v3 v3.0.1**: MIT / Apache License 2.0

The upstream NOTICE for `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` states: Copyright 2011-2016
Canonical Ltd. Its Apache License 2.0 terms and complete NOTICE text are retained in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`.

The offline bundle (`proxyscene_bundle_linux_*.tar.gz`) also **redistributes** the
following third-party component under its own copyright and license:

- **Xray-core v26.3.27** (the `xray` executable, source commit
  `d2758a023cd7f4174a5a5fa4ff66e487d4342ba0`)
  - Project: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core
  - License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
  - Its project license is retained as `LICENSE-Xray`. Exact versions, Go module sums,
    licenses, and notices for the 34 modules linked into the ELF are retained in
    `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES-Xray`.
  - `xray_source_v26.3.27.tar.gz` in the same immutable Release contains the exact Xray
    source and the Go proxy source zip, go.mod, and version metadata for all 34 modules.
    Retrieval details are retained in `SOURCE-Xray`.

The generated routing configuration does not use `geoip.dat` or `geosite.dat`, so
proxyscene no longer extracts, installs, or redistributes those third-party rule data files
from the Xray Release archive.

When redistributing this bundle you must keep this notice and comply with the licenses
